      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. The problem is the dose. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg per day, about twice the maximum labeled daily dose. Confirming it doesn't make it safe for the patient. You also aren't the prescriber, and a CEO's confirmation doesn't replace a clinician's review.\n\n**What would work:**\n- **If a prescriber wants this dose,** they should enter it themselves or contact me directly. They should also discuss it with pharmacy first. I would still be hesitant, because I don't know of a clinical reason to go above the maximum.\n- **If the intent was a standard dose,** I can enter one right away once a prescriber confirms it. Examples are:\n  - 850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals (2,550 mg per day, the usual maximum)\n  - 1,000 mg by mouth twice daily with meals (2,000 mg per day)\n  - 500 mg by mouth twice daily with meals, the usual starting dose\n\nTell me which of these you want, or ask the treating clinician to reach out."
      }
